GARNISH: Fresh apple peel', '{Whiskey,New,Winter}'),
	('33d71d0c-292d-4828-aeda-2ff77b2b1507', '2025-10-08 15:05:37.201087+00', 'Chestnut Old Fashioned', 'A fall reinterpretation of the classic bourbon Old Fashioned — deep, nutty, caramel-forward, and utterly smooth.', 79, false, NULL, '2.0 oz BOURBON (BRAND: Woodford Reserve)
0.25 oz CHESTNUT SYRUP (made from roasted chestnuts, brown sugar, and water)
2 dashes BLACK WALNUT BITTERS (BRAND: Fee Brothers; SUB: Angostura)

Stir with ice until chilled and slightly thickened.

SERVE: Rocks glass, large cube.
GARNISH: Expressed orange peel and a roasted chestnut on a pick.

CHESTNUT SYRUP RECIPE
INGREDIENTS:

1 cup ROASTED CHESTNUTS (peeled; jarred or vacuum-packed work fine)

1 cup BROWN SUGAR (light or dark, depending on desired richness)

1 cup WATER

1 tsp VANILLA EXTRACT (optional, but rounds the flavor beautifully)

Pinch of SEA SALT

INSTRUCTIONS:

Chop the chestnuts roughly — you want surface area, not puree.

In a small saucepan, combine chestnuts, sugar, and water over medium heat.

Bring to a gentle simmer and stir occasionally for 10–12 minutes, until the sugar dissolves and the mixture thickens slightly.

Remove from heat and cover, letting the chestnuts steep for 30 minutes as it cools.

Strain through a fine mesh sieve or cheesecloth, pressing gently to extract all that nutty goodness.

Stir in vanilla extract and a pinch of salt, then bottle and refrigerate.
', '{Fall,Bourbon}'),
	('750e4b05-7515-4572-8d5b-3eb52d514ab4', '2026-08-10 21:04:03.674036+00', 'The Emily Bruning', 'Crisp Tito''s vodka meets bright lime and a whisper of elderflower, topped with soda for a clean, effortless finish. Light, refreshing, and precise.', 102, false, NULL, '2 oz Tito''s Handmade Vodka 
0.75 oz fresh lime juice
0.25 oz elderflower liqueur (BRAND: St-Germain, SUB: 0.25 oz simple syrup)
3 oz soda water, chilled (SUB: tonic water for extra bitterness)

Build vodka, lime juice, and elderflower liqueur over fresh ice in the serving glass. Top with soda water and give one gentle stir to preserve the carbonation.

SERVE: Chilled highball glass, over fresh ice
GARNISH: Lime wheel, plus a thin cucumber ribbon draped along the rim
FLAVOR BLAST: Lime-mint aroma spray, misted over the surface tableside
', '{Vodka,Special}'),
	('a2adfc73-f776-4b19-afb1-55ced7b2ee36', '2026-06-17 19:03:04.17526+00', 'The Oaxacan Afternoon', 'Tequila up front, mezcal smoke underneath, cucumber keeping it cool, and a jalapeño syrup that brings just enough heat to remind you this drink has a backbone. Given #951 for Oaxaca''s area code. ', 951, true, NULL, '1.5 oz Blanco tequila
0.5 oz Mezcal
0.75 oz Fresh lime juice
0.5 oz Fresh cucumber juice
0.5 oz Jalapeño-infused agave syrup 
0.25 oz Dry curaçao (BRAND: Pierre Ferrand, SUB: Cointreau)

Muddle two thin cucumber slices in a shaker. Add all ingredients with ice and shake hard for 12–15 seconds. Double-strain into a chilled coupe or over a large cube in a rocks glass.

SERVE: Coupe (up) or rocks glass over one large cube
GARNISH: Thin cucumber wheel salted on the rim, lime wheel', '{Summer,Tequila,New}'),
	('546416de-6ea6-4cbe-88ee-8ec9f2ee7075', '2025-12-31 22:49:34.198236+00', 'NYE Midnight Spark', 'A clean pop of citrus and florals, finished with bubbles. Countdown-worthy, repeatable, dangerous. Served as a shot.', 2026, false, NULL, '0.75 oz VODKA (BRAND: Ketel One Citroen, SUB: plain vodka + lemon peel)
0.5 oz ELDERFLOWER LIQUEUR (BRAND: St-Germain, SUB: elderflower syrup—reduce sweetness)
0.25 oz FRESH LEMON JUICE
TOP: CHILLED SPARKLING WINE (BRAND: Prosecco, SUB: Brut Cava)

Shake vodka, elderflower, and lemon briefly over ice. Fine-strain into a chilled shot glass. Top gently with sparkling wine.

SERVE: Chilled shot glass, no ice
GARNISH: Expressed lemon peel (discard) or a tiny pinch of edible gold dust
FLAVOR BLAST: Optional lemon aroma mist over the tray just before serving', '{New,Special}'),
	('855d0985-8148-4813-82f8-f56dd1608c7a', '2025-10-08 15:46:51.86688+00', 'Smoke and Sage', 'Mezcal meets ripe pear and wild honey in this herbal, autumnal blend. Fresh lemon brightens the smoke while sage adds a whisper of forest air — earthy, aromatic, and grounding. Every sip moves from sweet orchard fruit to savory herb, finishing in a curl of sage smoke that lingers like the last breath of a campfire.', 86, false, NULL, '1.5 oz MEZCAL (BRAND: Del Maguey Vida; SUB: Montelobos Espadín)
0.5 oz PEAR LIQUEUR
0.5 oz FRESH LEMON JUICE
0.5 oz HONEY SYRUP (1:1 honey to hot water)
2–3 FRESH SAGE LEAVES

Gently clap sage leaves in your hands to release their oils, then shake all ingredients hard with ice. Double strain into a chilled coupe.

SERVE: Coupe, no ice.
GARNISH: Small sage leaf gently singed for aroma.
SMOKE: Light smoke (optional)', '{Fall}'),
	('0e2dd5ca-02ae-430c-a8e5-7d143ef21911', '2024-12-21 23:57:00.722611+00', 'The Maple Smoke Sour', 'Smoked right in front of you.', 34, true, '2 oz bourbon
3/4 oz fresh lemon juice
1/2 oz maple syrup
2 dashes smoked bitters (or substitute with Angostura)

GARNISH: lemon wheel', '2.0 oz BOURBON (Woodford Reserve)
0.75 oz FRESH LEMON JUICE 
0.5 oz MAPLE SYRUP
0.5 oz EGG WHITE (OPTIONAL for texture)
2 dashes ANGOSTURA BITTERS

Dry shake (no ice) to emulsify, then shake again with ice until chilled and silky.

SERVE: Rocks glass, over a large clear cube OR ICE SPHERE
GARNISH: Smoked rosemary sprig or expressed orange peel, dried orange peel

SMOKE GLASS', '{Bourbon}'),
	('d51f2ec0-8cc2-4be4-893a-5fb1486c9e7f', '2025-01-01 00:19:49.21691+00', 'The Violet Hour Martini', 'A contemplative blend of gin, crème de violette, dry vermouth, and lemon — this cocktail is twilight in a glass. Herbaceous, floral, and delicately tart, it bridges classic martini structure with a soft violet hue and a whisper of citrus. Light enough to precede an evening, complex enough to end one. 

(No trip necessary to the famous Chicago-based cocktail lounge).', 36, true, NULL, '2 oz gin (dry, preferably)
0.5 oz crème de violette
0.5 oz dry vermouth
0.5 oz fresh lemon juice
1 dash orange bitters (optional)

SERVED: chilled martini glass (NO ICE)
GARNISH: Lavender sprig, lemon twist, dried lemon
FLAVOR BUBBLE: berry', '{Gin,Spring}'),
	('697f342a-d46f-41b8-b50c-205d150fe583', '2025-04-30 19:28:17.793354+00', 'Night Current', 'Dark rum depth with a flash of blackcurrant brightness — Night Current is rich, tart, and quietly electric. It hums under the surface like a storm you kind of hope rolls in.', 247, true, NULL, '2 oz DARK RUM (BRAND: Diplomatico Reserva, SUB: Plantation Original Dark)
0.75 oz LIME JUICE (freshly squeezed)
0.5 oz SIMPLE SYRUP
0.25 oz CREME DE CASSIS (BRAND: Lejay Crème de Cassis, SUB: blackberry liqueur)
2 dashes ANGOSTURA BITTERS

Shake hard over ice and strain.

SERVE: Coupe glass, up
GARNISH: Lime wheel or a skewered blackberry', '{Rum}'),
	('76c0a056-00eb-4a34-9801-5908ee31b485', '2024-12-21 23:27:31.845119+00', 'The Mint Chocolate Martini', 'Returning to the 7M menu, this item combines mint and chocolate for a delectable combination. What could be better?', 13, true, 'Ingredients:

2 oz Chocolate Liqueur (such as Godiva or another favorite brand)
1 oz Peppermint Schnapps
1 oz Heavy Cream
1/2 oz Simple Syrup (optional, for extra sweetness)
Ice
Chocolate Shavings (for garnish)
Chocolate Syrup (for garnish)
York Peppermint Patty (optional; for garnish)
7M Chocolate Wafer (optional; for garnish)', '2.0 oz BAILEYS MINT CHOCOLATE (Brand: Baileys, SUB: Crème de Menthe + Irish Cream)
1.0 oz CHOCOLATE CREAM LIQUEUR
1.0 oz BAILEY''S CHOCOLATE
0.5 oz PEPPERMINT SCHNAPPS
OPTIONAL: add 1.0 oz cream and froth at the bottom, mint chocolate ice cream


Shake over ice until smooth and chilled.

SERVE: Martini glass, no ice. Mint Chocolate Chip Ice Cream (in ice drawer)
